mysql.procs_priv rows are written with the user name re-encoded from latin1

replace_routine_table() stores Host, Db, User, Routine_name and Grantor into
mysql.procs_priv tagged as latin1, while replace_table_table() (tables_priv),
replace_column_table() and replace_db_table() tag them as system_charset_info
(utf8mb3). For an account whose name has bytes outside ASCII the row therefore
holds the UTF-8 bytes converted a second time (D1 82 for "т" becomes
C3 91 E2 80 9A): SHOW GRANTS lists the EXECUTE grant until the next FLUSH
PRIVILEGES or restart, after which the privilege tables are re-read and the
grant belongs to a user that does not exist, so the real account loses
EXECUTE on every routine. DROP FUNCTION / DROP PROCEDURE go through the same
function and only find the re-encoded rows, so a row corrected by hand stays
behind as an orphan and REVOKE ALL on that account fails with ER_NONEXISTING_GRANT.

The line is unchanged from MySQL 5.5 through MariaDB 13.0 / main (2026-10).
Reproduced with the official 12.3.3 binaries:

  SET NAMES utf8mb3;
  CREATE USER 'тест'@'%';
  CREATE FUNCTION t.f() RETURNS INT DETERMINISTIC RETURN 1;
  GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION t.f TO 'тест'@'%';
  SELECT HEX(User) FROM mysql.procs_priv WHERE Routine_name='f';
  -- C391E2809AC390C2B5C391C281C391E2809A, expected D182D0B5D181D182
  FLUSH PRIVILEGES; SHOW GRANTS FOR 'тест'@'%';   -- EXECUTE gone

Store the five strings with system_charset_info, as the other grant tables do.

SCteam, 2026-10-18 (holong T-137 / T-161 / T-250).

--- a/sql/sql_acl.cc
+++ b/sql/sql_acl.cc
@@ -6282,11 +6282,11 @@
 
